Windows Registry Editor Version 5.00
; ===================================================================
; DisableMPO.reg
; Disables Multi-Plane Overlay (MPO) in the Windows Desktop Window
; Manager (DWM).
;
; WHY: MPO is a hardware-accelerated display composition path used by
; the GPU driver and DWM. On some GPU/driver/monitor combinations it
; causes intermittent input lag, dropped clicks, cursor stutter, and
; "ghost" double-clicks because the compositor hands frames (and the
; cursor plane) between hardware overlays. The problem lives BELOW
; the service layer, which is why it survives Safe Mode.
;
; HOW: OverlayTestMode = 5 forces DWM to fall back to the legacy
; (non-MPO) composition path. Same switch Microsoft Support uses for
; MPO-related flicker/lag on Windows 10 2004+ and Windows 11.
;
; SCOPE: HKLM (machine-wide). Requires FULL REBOOT to take effect.
;
; TO REVERT: Apply ReEnableMPO.reg and reboot.
; ===================================================================
[HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\SOFTWARE\Microsoft\Windows\Dwm]
"OverlayTestMode"=dword:00000005